I added two register commands: one merges the register branch into develop one way, and one flags register files edited directly on develop. Both do nothing unless `register_sync` is enabled, which it isn't in this project's config yet. I didn't change `lefthook.yml` or `.github/` (both protected), so the check isn't in any hook or CI yet. The proposed changes are in the ticket.

**What I added**
- **`register branch-merge`**: fetches the remote register branch and merges it into the current branch with `--no-ff`. It refuses to start if there are staged changes, a merge already in progress, uncommitted edits to register files, a detached HEAD, or if the register branch touches files outside bookkeeping. If the merge conflicts, it aborts the merge and says why.
- **`register branch-guard`**: `--staged` checks the index (for pre-commit) and `--range <range>` checks a range of commits (for pre-push or CI). A change to a register file is allowed only if its content matches what a merged-in parent got from the register branch. Commits on the register branch itself are not checked, so register changes that reach a feature branch through develop pass. Squashed or hand-made edits fail.
- **Runner**: `exec run --register --worktree` now merges the register branch before it creates the worktree. If that merge fails, it stops without creating the worktree.

**Decisions and reasons**
- **CLI and runner rather than GitHub Actions.** Actions would need the right to push past develop's PR protection, which is roughly the GitHub App setup that `PJR-2TX0` rejected. It would also need changes to the protected `.github/`. With the CLI, each person uses their own credentials and the merge commits reach develop through normal PRs. Develop never changes register files, so these merges don't conflict.
- **Only register runs get the automatic merge.** Schedule runs already read their events from the register branch since `PJR-N5J8`, so I left them alone.
- **The check shouldn't go into the hook yet.** The runner still writes ticket updates on the exec branch and brings them into develop. Once the check is on, those updates count as violations. It should be added after the runner writes to the register branch (option 2a in `PJR-2TX0`).

**Proposed hook and CI changes (not applied)**
- `lefthook.yml` pre-commit, entry `register-branch-guard`: `[ ! -f dist/specdojo.js ] || node dist/specdojo.js register branch-guard --project prj-0001 --staged`
- CI: on pushes and PRs to develop, run `specdojo register branch-guard --project prj-0001 --range <base>..<head>`. The job needs `fetch-depth: 0` and must also fetch the register branch.
- People with `register_sync` on run `specdojo register branch-merge --project prj-0001` before they start work. I decided against putting this in a post-checkout hook because it would create merge commits without anyone asking.

**Verification:** I ran the new integration test file `tests/src/register/register-branch-merge.integration.test.ts` on its own and all 6 tests passed. They cover repeated merges without conflicts, a feature branch picking up register changes through develop, catching direct edits (staged and committed), aborting a conflicting merge, refusing changes outside bookkeeping, and doing nothing without `register_sync`. `npm run validate:history-links` and `npm run check:src-imports` passed. A type check of `src` was clean, and ESLint on the changed files had no errors. It did give two warnings about function length in `register-worktree.ts`. One is for `runSingleRegisterItemWorktree`, which my 19 lines made longer, and that function was already over the limit. The full typecheck, lint, unit and integration runs are left to the runner.

I also updated the command reference, the register operation guide and the Git branching standard. The ticket now has its work table, results, decisions and the CHANGELOG draft (Added, v0.10.0).

Changed files:
- `src/shared/register-merge.ts` (new)
- `src/register/branch-commands.ts` (new)
- `src/register/register.ts`
- `src/exec/run/register-worktree.ts`
- `tests/src/register/register-branch-merge.integration.test.ts` (new)
- `docs/ja/specdojo/references/command-reference.md`
- `docs/ja/specdojo/guides/register-operation-guide.md`
- `docs/ja/specdojo/standards/git-branching-standard.md`
- `docs/ja/projects/prj-0001/controls/project-register/pjr-1jf6-register-branch-merge-into-develop.md`

